{
  "id": "jj9a16m",
  "title": "CHAPTER 12: PRACTICE QUESTIONS AND MODEL PAPERS",
  "order": 11,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b916y3g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.1 Tamil Nadu History – Practice Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Who built the Brihadeeswarar Temple at Thanjavur?",
      "id": "c35buvz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Rajendra Chola I  (b) Rajaraja Chola I  (c) Kulottunga Chola I  (d) Vijayalaya Chola",
      "id": "cn1cev7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (b) Rajaraja Chola I",
      "id": "e7ow1ah"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. In which year was Fort St. George established at Madras?",
      "id": "mrbk5be"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) 1600  (b) 1623  (c) 1639  (d) 1664",
      "id": "kcilltw"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (c) 1639",
      "id": "d0kuf5s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. The Tirukkural was written by:",
      "id": "4chaanw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Kambar  (b) Ilango Adigal  (c) Thiruvalluvar  (d) Sekkizhar",
      "id": "us3knqh"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (c) Thiruvalluvar",
      "id": "87png7e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. The Shore Temple at Mahabalipuram was built during which dynasty?",
      "id": "m4pd2au"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Pandyas  (b) Pallavas  (c) Cheras  (d) Cholas",
      "id": "rwarhky"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (b) Pallavas",
      "id": "r9bfxvs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "5. Veerapandiya Kattabomman was hanged at:",
      "id": "2asbmp1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Tirunelveli  (b) Thoothukudi  (c) Kayathar  (d) Madurai",
      "id": "rsl87f2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (c) Kayathar",
      "id": "yqf9t33"
    },
    {
      "id": "w8fjlq9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.2 Tamil Nadu Geography – Practice Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "6. The highest peak in Tamil Nadu is:",
      "id": "y4kumi8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Anaimudi  (b) Doddabetta  (c) Makurti  (d) Kolukkumalai",
      "id": "ig6wl12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   Answer: (b) Doddabetta (2,637 m) in the Nilgiris",
      "id": "xq0b2oh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "7. The Mettur Dam is built across which river?",
      "id": "dunlws8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Bhavani  (b) Noyyal  (c) Kaveri  (d) Palar",
      "id": "ejvaqkp"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (c) Kaveri",
      "id": "gfqt9bv"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "8. Which district is famous for garnet mining?",
      "id": "zeb0gxt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Salem  (b) Thoothukudi  (c) Namakkal  (d) Erode",
      "id": "y5jacfn"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (b) Thoothukudi (Tiruchendur)",
      "id": "msdxx0s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "9. Vedanthangal Bird Sanctuary is in which district?",
      "id": "aifcdk8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "   (a) Tiruvallur  (b) Kancheepuram  (c) Chengalpattu  (d) Villupuram",
      "id": "odxoyhx"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "   Answer: (c) Chengalpattu",
      "id": "cmd7icn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "10. Tamil Nadu's state animal is:",
      "id": "e1agwzf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Elephant  (b) Nilgiri Tahr  (c) Lion-tailed Macaque  (d) Tiger",
      "id": "ka8gc5z"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (b) Nilgiri Tahr",
      "id": "ptoyt9e"
    },
    {
      "id": "9dcj6us",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.3 Polity – Practice Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "11. The Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly has how many seats?",
      "id": "kf30dco"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) 196  (b) 225  (c) 234  (d) 250",
      "id": "neb3ine"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (c) 234",
      "id": "cdvyr82"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "12. Which constitutional article deals with the establishment of Public Service Commissions?",
      "id": "xjn4usc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Article 280  (b) Article 315  (c) Article 324  (d) Article 343",
      "id": "1s0u4om"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (b) Article 315",
      "id": "18km4x1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "13. 'Socialist' and 'Secular' were added to the Preamble by which amendment?",
      "id": "jw6mdg2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) 40th  (b) 42nd  (c) 44th  (d) 52nd",
      "id": "1u7v3lt"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (b) 42nd Amendment (1976)",
      "id": "jamtz25"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "14. The Madras High Court was established in:",
      "id": "mlr94c0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) 1857  (b) 1862  (c) 1885  (d) 1920",
      "id": "tglzpvm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (b) 1862",
      "id": "92y3qw3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "15. Which district in Tamil Nadu is headquarters of Kalakkad-Mundanthurai Tiger Reserve?",
      "id": "m2u91sx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Madurai  (b) Tirunelveli  (c) Thoothukudi  (d) Virudhunagar",
      "id": "vkfasjt"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (b) Tirunelveli",
      "id": "7kfv39y"
    },
    {
      "id": "uclz3no",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.4 General Science – Practice Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "16. The chemical formula of baking soda is:",
      "id": "dz4j4u9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Na2CO3  (b) NaCl  (c) NaHCO3  (d) CaCO3",
      "id": "rs8rdeq"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (c) NaHCO3 (Sodium bicarbonate)",
      "id": "eajc9l4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "17. Who discovered the Raman Effect?",
      "id": "jajpved"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Homi Bhabha  (b) C.V. Raman  (c) A.P.J. Abdul Kalam  (d) Vikram Sarabhai",
      "id": "x8xt787"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    Answer: (b) C.V. Raman (1928); Nobel Prize 1930",
      "id": "x35b8tt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "18. Chandrayaan-3 successfully landed on the Moon's south pole in:",
      "id": "nr5g4wo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) 2021  (b) 2022  (c) 2023  (d) 2024",
      "id": "t8uqw9o"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    Answer: (c) 2023 (August 23, 2023)",
      "id": "fj68ytk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "19. pH of pure water is:",
      "id": "vedj01t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) 0  (b) 5  (c) 7  (d) 14",
      "id": "i0na6m4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "    Answer: (c) 7",
      "id": "flh9dae"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "20. The first biosphere reserve in India is:",
      "id": "93s6v6i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    (a) Sunderbans  (b) Gulf of Mannar  (c) Nilgiri  (d) Nanda Devi",
      "id": "uymw31a"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "    Answer: (c) Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve (1986)",
      "id": "hpwkf4r"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": false
}